"] " both qualified for the quarters from the same repêchage. Germany’s reigning world champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/143279"} "Emma Hinze"] " had already collected a team sprint silver in Tokyo, but she made hard work in qualifying for the keirin quarter-finals, finishing second in her heat. Her sprint partner " [:a {:href "/athletes/143282"} "Lea-Sophie Friedrich"] " won her heat against Shmelyova."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/130229"} "Katy Marchant"] " was relegated to fifth in her opening heat for entering the sprinter’s lane when the opponent was already there. She won her repêchage, however, and went through to the quarter-finals. China’s recently crowned sprint champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/121948"} "Gong Jinjie"] " qualified for the quarters while her team-mate " [:a {:href "/athletes/141668"} "Bao Shanju"] " finished last in her repêchage. Shmelyova, McCulloch and Hinze were all eliminated at the semi-final stage."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final was a thrilling six lap race and Dutch rider " [:a {:href "/athletes/145457"} "Shanne Braspennincx"] ", who led from the front, won by 0.061 from New Zealand’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/145727"} "Ellesse Andrews"] ", with Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/141389"} "Lauriane Genest"] " taking the bronze medal. It was a remarkable victory for Braspennincx who suffered a heart attack in 2015 and now was an Olympic champion."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "R1 Rep"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/145457"} "Shanne Braspennincx"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "at 0.105 (3 h4)"] [:td {} "11.135 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "11.334 (1 